  "prompt": "You are an expert JavaScript developer. Create a single-page, standalone HTML document containing a fully playable \"Tango\" logic puzzle game.\n\nSTRICT TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n1. ALL HTML, CSS, and JavaScript must be contained within a single file. No external libraries.\n2. Do NOT output markdown code blocks (```html). Start exactly with <!DOCTYPE html> and end with </html>.\n\nTHEME & VISUALS:\n1. The game must look polished and modern, utilizing a clean, balanced interface.\n2. The grid must be 6x6 cells.\n3. The two playing symbols MUST be the Fire emoji (\ud83d\udd25) and the Ice Cube emoji (\ud83e\uddca).\n4. Constraint markers must clearly sit on the borders between adjacent cells using an Equals sign (=) or a Cross (\u00d7).\n\nCORE GAMEPLAY RULES:\n1. Row and Column Balance: Every row and every column must contain exactly three \ud83d\udd25 and three \ud83e\uddca.\n2. No Three in a Row: You cannot place three identical symbols adjacent to each other horizontally or vertically.\n3. Constraint Markers:\n   - '=' (Equals): The two adjacent cells must contain the same symbol.\n   - '\u00d7' (Cross): The two adjacent cells must contain opposite symbols.\n4. Interactivity: Clicking a cell should cycle its state: Empty -> \ud83d\udd25 -> \ud83e\uddca -> Empty.\n\nBACK-END LOGIC & PROCEDURAL GENERATION SPECS:\nThe game MUST generate a brand new, random, playable board on every page load. Implement the generation using this sequence:\n1. Solution Generation (Backtracking): Write a recursive backtracking function to generate a fully populated, valid 6x6 grid that obeys the Balance and No-Three-In-A-Row rules. \n2. Constraint Placement: Once a valid solved board exists, randomly select 6 to 8 pairs of adjacent cells. If the cells share the same symbol, place an '=' marker between them. If they are different, place an '\u00d7' marker.\n3. Puzzle Creation: After placing constraints, randomly clear (empty) 70% of the cells, leaving a few starting symbols and the constraint markers as hints for the player.\n4. Validation: Implement a \"Check Solution\" button that compares the user's current grid against the underlying rules (Balance, No-Three-In-A-Row, and Constraints). Highlight any errors in red.\n\nEnsure the state management clearly separates the \"solution board\" from the \"player board\", and that markers overlay the grid lines cleanly using CSS absolute positioning or a highly refined Grid layout.\n",
  "rawOutput": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>Tango Puzzle</title>\n<style>\n  body { margin:0; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; background:#f5f5f5; }\n  .grid {\n    display:grid;\n    grid-template-columns:repeat(6,100px);\n    gap:1px;\n    background:#fff;\n    padding:10px;\n    box-sizing:border-box;\n  }\n  .cell {\n    width:100px; height:100px; border:1px solid #999; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;\n    user-select:none; cursor:pointer;\n    font-size:1.5rem;\n  }\n  .constraint {\n    position:absolute; pointer-events:none; background:rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"grid\" id=\"grid\"></div>\n<button id=\"checkBtn\">Check Solution</button>\n\n<script>\nconst symbols = ['\ud83d\udd25', '\ud83e\uddca', '']; // fire, ice, empty\nconst markerSymbols = ['=', '\u00d7'];\nlet solvedBoard = null;\nlet playerBoard = null;\nlet markers = {}; // cellIndex => markerSymbol\n\nfunction generateRandomBoard() {\n  const board = Array.from({length:36}, () => '');\n  for (let i=0;i<36;i++) {\n    const s = symbols[Math.floor(Math.random()*3)];\n    board[i] = s;\n  }\n  return board;\n}\n\nfunction placeConstraints(board) {\n  const pairs = [];\n  let attempts = 0;\n  const totalPairs = 6 + Math.floor(Math.random()*8); // 6-14\n  while (pairs.length < totalPairs && attempts < 10000) {\n    attempts++;\n    const pairs = [];\n    for (let i=0;i<totalPairs;i++) {\n      const row = Math.floor(Math.random()*6);\n      const col = Math.floor(Math.random()*6);\n      const right = (col+1)%6;\n      const down = (row+1)%6;\n      if (Math.random()<0.5) {\n        const type = symbols[Math.floor(Math.random()*2)];\n        pairs.push({cell: row*6+col, type});\n      } else {\n        const type = symbols[Math.floor(Math.random()*2)];\n        pairs.push({cell: row*6+col, type});\n      }\n    }\n    // ensure we have distinct pairs\n    if (pairs.length >= totalPairs) break;\n  }\n  return pairs;\n}\n\nfunction clearCells(board) {\n  for (let i=0;i<36;i++) board[i] = '';\n}\n\nfunction randomizeStartBoard(board) {\n  const keep = Math.floor(0.3*36) + 1; // 2-3 symbols\n  const indices = Array.from({length:36}, (_,i) => i);\n  shuffle(indices);\n  for (let i=0;i<keep;i++) {\n    const idx = indices[Math.floor(Math.random()*indices.length)];\n    board[idx] = symbols[Math.floor(Math.random()*2)];\n  }\n  return keep;\n}\n\nfunction shuffle(arr) {\n  for (let i=arr.length-1;i>=0;i--) {\n    const j = Math.floor(Math.random()*i+1);\n    [arr[i], arr[j]] = [arr[j], arr[i]];\n  }\n}\n\nfunction validateBoard(board) {\n  const errors=[];\n\n  // rows\n  for (let r=0;r<6;r++) {\n    let cntFire=0,cntIce=0;\n    for (let c=0;c<6;c++) {\n      const cell = board[r*6+c];\n      if (cell==='\ud83d\udd25') cntFire++;\n      else if (cell==='\ud83e\uddca') cntIce++;\n    }\n    if (cntFire!=3 || cntIce!=3) errors.push(`Row ${r+1}: not 3 fire/ice`);\n    // no three in a row horizontally\n    for (let c=0;c<5;c++) {\n      const a = board[r*6+c];\n      const b = board[r*6+c+1];\n      const c2 = board[r*6+c+2];\n      if (a && a===b && b===c2) errors.push(`Row ${r+1}, col ${c+1}: three in a row`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // columns\n  for (let c=0;c<6;c++) {\n    let cntFire=0,cntIce=0;\n    for (let r=0;r<6;r++) {\n      const cell = board[r*6+c];\n      if (cell==='\ud83d\udd25') cntFire++;\n      else if (cell==='\ud83e\uddca') cntIce++;\n    }\n    if (cntFire!=3 || cntIce!=3) errors.push(`Col ${c+1}: not 3 fire/ice`);\n    // no three in a row vertically\n    for (let r=0;r<5;r++) {\n      const a = board[r*6+c];\n      const b = board[r+1*6+c];\n      const c2 = board[r+2*6+c];\n      if (a && a===b && b===c2) errors.push(`Col ${c+1}, row ${r+1}: three in a row`);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // constraint markers\n  for (const [cellIdx,type] of Object.entries(markers)) {\n    const r = Math.floor(cellIdx/6), c = cellIdx%6;\n    const left = c*100;\n    const top = r*100;\n    if (type === '=') {\n      if (board[r*6+c] && board[(r*6)+(c+1)] && board[r*6+c] !== board[(r*6)+(c+1)]) {\n        errors.push(`Marker on right edge of ${r+1}-${c+1}: same symbol required`);\n      }\n    } else { // '\u00d7'\n      if (board[r*6+c] && board[(r*6)+(c+1)] && board[r*6+c] === board[(r*6)+(c+1)]) {\n        errors.push(`Marker on right edge of ${r+1}-${c+1}: opposite symbols required`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return errors;\n}\n\nfunction render() {\n  const grid = document.getElementById('grid');\n  grid.innerHTML='';\n\n  for (let r=0;r<6;r++) {\n    for (let c=0;c<6;c++) {\n      const cellIdx = r*6+c;\n      const cell = solvedBoard[cellIdx];\n      let cellStr = '';\n      if (cell==='') cellStr = '';\n      else cellStr = cell;\n\n      const cellDiv = document.createElement('div');\n      cellDiv.className='cell';\n      cellDiv.textContent = cellStr;\n      cellDiv.dataset.index = cellIdx;\n      grid.appendChild(cellDiv);\n\n      // add constraint marker if present\n      if (markers[cellIdx]) {\n        const marker = document.createElement('span');\n        marker.className='constraint';\n        marker.dataset.marker = markers[cellIdx];\n        marker.style.left = `${c*100}px`;\n        marker.style.top = `${r*100}px`;\n        grid.appendChild(marker);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction toggleSymbol(cellIdx) {\n  const cellDivs = document.querySelectorAll('.cell');\n  cellDivs.forEach(div=>{\n    if (div.dataset.index===cellIdx) {\n      div.textContent = symbols[Math.floor(Math.random()*2)];\n      return;\n    }\n  });\n}\n\nfunction placeConstraintsOnSolution() {\n  const pairs = placeConstraints(solvedBoard);\n  pairs.forEach(p=>{\n    const left = p.cell;\n    const right = (p.cell+1)%6;\n    const type = symbols[Math.floor(Math.random()*2)];\n    const markerDiv = document.createElement('span');\n    markerDiv.className='constraint';\n    markerDiv.dataset.marker = type;\n    markerDiv.style.left = `${right*100}px`;\n    markerDiv.style.top = `${left/6*100}px`;\n    grid.appendChild(markerDiv);\n    markers[p.cell] = type;\n  });\n}\n\nfunction checkSolution() {\n  const errors = validateBoard(playerBoard);\n  if (errors.length) {\n    document.body.style.backgroundColor = '#ffcccc';\n    errors.forEach(e=> console.log(e));\n  } else {\n    document.body.style.backgroundColor = '#fff';\n  }\n  document.getElementById('checkBtn').textContent = errors.length ? 'Errors' : 'Check Solution';\n}\n\nfunction startGame() {\n  solvedBoard = generateRandomBoard();\n  randomizeStartBoard(solvedBoard);\n  playerBoard = randomizeStartBoard(solvedBoard);\n  placeConstraintsOnSolution();\n  clearCells(playerBoard);\n  render();\n}\n\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', startGame);\ndocument.getElementById('checkBtn').addEventListener('click', checkSolution);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>",
